      "text": "<think>\nI need to add the two numbers: 176,827,714 and 919,473,645.\n\nFirst, I'll add the numbers in the units place: 4 plus 5 equals 9.\n\nNext, I'll add the tens place: 1 plus 4 equals 5.\n\nThen, I'll add the hundreds place: 7 plus 3 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nMoving to the thousands place: 2 plus 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 9.\n\nFor the ten-thousands place: 8 plus 7 equals 15. I'll write down 5 and carry over 1.\n\nIn the hundred-thousands place: 7 plus 4 plus the carried-over 1 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1.\n\nNext, the millions place: 6 plus 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 16. I'll write down 6 and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, in the ten-millions place: 1 plus 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\nSince there are no more digits to add, I'll write down the carried-over 1.\n\nCombining all these results, the sum of 176,827,714 and 919,473,645 is 1,096,301,359.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\nWe need to find the sum of the two numbers:\n\n\\[\n176,\\!827,\\!714 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 919,\\!473,\\!645\n\\]\n\nLet's add them step by step:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}176,\\!827,\\!714 \\\\\n+919,\\!473,\\!645 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Step 1:** Add the units place:\n\n\\[\n4 + 5 = 9\n\\]\n\n**Step 2:** Add the tens place:\n\n\\[\n1 + 4 = 5\n\\]\n\n**Step 3:** Add the hundreds place:\n\n\\[\n7 + 3 = 10 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 0 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n\\]\n\n**Step 4:** Add the thousands place:\n\n\\[\n2 + 6 + 1 (\\text{carried over}) = 9\n\\]\n\n**Step 5:** Add the ten-thousands place:\n\n\\[\n8 + 7 = 15 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 5 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n\\]\n\n**Step 6:** Add the hundred-thousands place:\n\n\\[\n7 + 4 + 1 (\\text{carried over}) = 12 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 2 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n\\]\n\n**Step 7:** Add the millions place:\n\n\\[\n6 + 9 + 1 (\\text{carried over}) = 16 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 6 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n\\]\n\n**Step 8:** Add the ten-millions place:\n\n\\[\n1 + 9 + 1 (\\text{carried over}) = 11 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 1 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n\\]\n\n**Step 9:** Since there are no more digits to add, write down the carried-over **1**.\n\n**Final Sum:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1,\\!096,\\!301,\\!359}\n\\]",
