      "text": "<think>\nI need to add the two numbers 949,427,186 and 968,286,280. I'll start by aligning them by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nFirst, I'll add the units place: 6 + 0 equals 6.\n\nNext, I'll move to the tens place: 8 + 8 equals 16. I'll write down 6 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nFor the hundreds place: 1 + 2 plus the carried-over 1 equals 4.\n\nContinuing this process, I'll add each subsequent pair of digits, carrying over any excess to the next higher place value as needed.\n\nAfter adding all the digits, I'll combine the results to find the total sum.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo find the sum of **949,427,186** and **968,286,280**, follow these steps:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}949,\\!427,\\!186 \\\\\n+968,\\!286,\\!280 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Step 1:** Add the numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (units place).\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}949,\\!427,\\!186 \\\\\n+968,\\!286,\\!280 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Step 2:** Add the units place:\n\\[\n6 + 0 = 6\n\\]\n\n**Step 3:** Add the tens place:\n\\[\n8 + 8 = 16 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 6 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n\\]\n\n**Step 4:** Add the hundreds place:\n\\[\n1 + 2 + 1 (\\text{carried over}) = 4\n\\]\n\n**Step 5:** Add the thousands place:\n\\[\n9 + 6 = 15 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 5 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n\\]\n\n**Step 6:** Add the ten-thousands place:\n\\[\n4 + 8 + 1 (\\text{carried over}) = 13 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 3 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n\\]\n\n**Step 7:** Add the hundred-thousands place:\n\\[\n7 + 2 + 1 (\\text{carried over}) = 10 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 0 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n\\]\n\n**Step 8:** Add the millions place:\n\\[\n4 + 8 + 1 (\\text{carried over}) = 13 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 3 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n\\]\n\n**Step 9:** Add the ten-millions place:\n\\[\n9 + 6 + 1 (\\text{carried over}) = 16 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 